content:
Help me define bounded contexts. Below I will provide domain information. 

#### Data:
These are the extracted objects and the subdomain grouping:
```json
{
  "subdomains": {
    "Ordering": {
      "objects": [
        "Customer",
        "Restaurant Staff Member",
        "Restaurant",
        "Food Order",
        "Meal"
      ]
    },
    "Customer Issues": {
      "objects": [
        "Support Agent",
        "Issue Report",
        "Refund"
      ]
    },
    "Delivery": {
      "objects": [
        "Delivery Driver",
        "Pick Up",
        "Meal Package",
        "Food Order",
        "Meal",
        "Delivery",
        "Delivery Status"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```
```json
{
  "domain objects": [
    {
      "name": "Customer",
      "description": "Person placing orders and receiving deliveries."
    },
    {
      "name": "Restaurant",
      "description": "Food provider offering meals to customers."
    },
    {
      "name": "Food Order",
      "description": "Order placed by a customer for a meal.",
      "attributes": [
        "Restaurant",
        "Meal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Meal",
      "description": "Prepared food item included in a food order."
    },
    {
      "name": "Meal Package",
      "description": "Packaged meal prepared for pickup.",
      "attributes": [
        "Food Order"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Pick Up",
      "description": "Event where a driver collects the meal package."
    },
    {
      "name": "Delivery Driver",
      "description": "Driver responsible for picking up and delivering orders."
    },
    {
      "name": "Delivery",
      "description": "Process of transporting a meal package to a customer.",
      "attributes": [
        "Delivery Status",
        "Meal Package"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Delivery Status",
      "description": "State of the delivery"
    },
    {
      "name": "Support Agent",
      "description": "Staff member resolving customer issues."
    },
    {
      "name": "Issue Report",
      "description": "Customer-submitted problem related to an order."
    },
    {
      "name": "Refund",
      "description": "Compensation issued to a customer for a valid issue."
    },
    {
      "name": "Restaurant Staff Member",
      "description": "Staff preparing and packaging food orders."
    }
  ]
}
```

#### Task:
- Assign the subdomains to bounded contexts. 
- Name the subdomain the bounded context might be derived from, it might also be multiple.
- Identify cases, where an object does not have a unified meaning across all bounded contexts and suggest a name change.
- Return the bounded contexts in json format. Here is an example for structuring the data:
```json
{
  "bounded contexts": {
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": []
    },
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "... -> ..."
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

Here are the bounded contexts: 
```json
{
  "bounded contexts": {
    "Ordering": {
      "derived from": "Ordering Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Customer",
        "Restaurant Staff Member",
        "Restaurant",
        "Food Order",
        "Meal"
      ],
      "name changes": []
    },
    "Customer Issues": {
      "derived from": "Customer Issues Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Support Agent",
        "Issue Report",
        "Refund"
      ],
      "name changes": []
    },
    "Delivery": {
      "derived from": "Delivery Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Delivery Driver",
        "Pick Up",
        "Meal Package",
        "Order Assignment",
        "Item",
        "Delivery",
        "Delivery Status"
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "Food Order -> Order Assignment",
        "Meal -> Item"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```
